<title>AUSTRALIA: Burson-Marsteller wins Telstra  pr deal.</title>
<headline>Burson-Marsteller wins Telstra  pr deal.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Finance Minister John Fahey said on Tuesday that public relations consultants Burson-Marsteller would be manage public relations issues surrounding the partial sale of telecoms carrier Telstra Corp.</p>
<p>&quot;Burson-Marsteller will provide retail marketing and issues management advice to the Commonwealth in relation to the partial sale of Telstra,&quot; Fahey said in a statement.</p>
<p>The government hopes to raise at least A$8.0 billion from the sale of one-third of Telstra. The sale is expected to take place before the end of calendar 1997.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
</text>
